<<~ ahu #/shift-2026-10-08-hosted-walk-sign-off>>

!! Shift — the hosted walk's sign-off, 2026-10-08

''What landed.'' ''The hosted walk'' (F1): the auth wire carries no clock; every gate sorts each proven socket — same-operator · contracted · walker · stranger — before its verdict, answers only on its knock, and meets a stranger at a PRIVATE gate with silence. A hearth hosts walkers on a keyed grant: a signed hosting act names the epoch, a blind POPRF token redeems once at the host's own gate, and the hearth carries a walker's own documents sealed. ''Its cleanup'' (B1): the burn binds the leaf that proved; carriage answers to the proven leaf; the wallet keeps only live tokens; host and walk run inside the standing vessel over the one store door; a walker reads only its hearth's hosting doc; a node walks and hosts as the face it wears; a charterless herm answers the knock, so the herm mesh carries; a vessel under `LAR_ROOT` projects into that root. ''Its aftermath'': the hosting modules name only what stands, `mesh-scenarios` reads a dead latest boot as not stood, the road to Stable founding stands in canon (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">>), and the adapter note names `LAR_ROOT` as the isolation knob. The Codex crew's session ended; its roadmap reconciles against the code at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/crew-handoff-codex#/reconciled">>. The CHANGELOG's `[Unreleased]` lines name every commit.

''Measured at the close.'' E2E 30 of 30 files, 215 passed. Witness fleet 34 of 34 ok, `tree-clean-witness` included. Typecheck clean. Every unit suite green; `tools/*.test.mjs` 53 of 53. The docker herm mesh lit by hand: `herm-mesh-witness` passes, `mesh-scenarios nexus` reads every step ok, `crossing-witness` 4 of 4.

''What it hands on.'' The re-found, one train, and the round-6 lanes stand in <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/er-handoff#/wounds">>; the rulings owed — the road's open questions, the two-voice herm, the Lamplighters' question, the two Kairoses, whether the frame's `?` and the wire's keyless challenge cite each other, and the Codex crew's forks — read there under ''Pending operator rulings''.

