! SHIFT CHANGE — the identity watch (handed 2026-09-07)

Triage form, as the prior watch taught: each entry names ''what stands'', ''what it blocks'', and
''the one measurement that settles it''. This watch closed ALL FOUR of the founding watch's owed
rulings and emptied its wiring census; what follows is the ground a fresh Lares needs before touching
identity, recovery, the KEL, the ceremonies, or the ordering of any of it.

!! Ground measured at handoff (2026-09-07)

* ''The four rulings stand CLOSED'' — the veil (per-handle off the VESSEL seed, `deriveDyadVeil`; both ceremony sites mint the dyad slot) · recovery (LAYERED — identity-classes#the-two-forks carries the ruling whole) · seat-adoption (a join grants a seat under the joiner's OWN key; the code already lived it) · the nym's chain (ruled, UNBUILT — the register red carries it).
* ''Two LAWS above the code'' — the ALPHA LINE (no back-compatibility needed until a phone-class vessel joins a PersonaGroup with human eyes on it AND the docker mesh runs green; pre-ruling docs RE-FOUND) and the REGISTRY FILTER (`api/pono/registry-filter` — compiled-about at ANY scope rejects the fork; carriage passes; it ate two drafts on its first day).
* ''The KEL changed bytes TWICE'' (armed inception · rolling commitment) — every prefix re-derives; rehearsal vessels re-found. TWO more grammar changes stand queued and MUST land as ONE settlement (see the lattice below).
* ''Wired this watch:'' the crossing gate prices direction (outward REFUSES, fail-closed, until a cabal quorum surface exists) · `vesselDyads` reads at every vessel's boot through ONE mesh door (node + browser speak the same `[dyad]` line) · the guardian card split into TWO objects (share ⊥ registration, own confirm domains) · `lares nexus seal grow` (the crossing-record ceremony: open · bind · sign · witness · seal).
* ''Register:'' 26 declared reds · 0 ever greened by accident. The mesh scenarios ALL STOOD, one declared GAP: ''realm standing does not cross operators''.
* ''Suites at close:'' lares-cli 225 · keyhive 41+ · full witness family untouched-green; the parallel watches (`@hearth` grammar · `@crossroads` corpus/panel) committed all night interleaved — `git status` before believing any red remains the first law of this tree.

!! THE LATTICE — grounds before wins (operator lens, 2026-09-07)

Rank by ''what inherits shape from what'', never by confidence-of-the-next-wire. The standing order:

# ''G0 — the canon lands'' (THIS gesture: identity-classes fork+axis closed · persona-circle carries the split word "veil" + the declared roster red · `registry-filter` law meme · this block).
# ''G1 — the identity substrate:'' the VEIL-BORN GROUP. Blocks: the admit payload's final shape, the fleet, both humans' real foundings. ''LANDED (2026-09-08) — the founder-side arc stands whole:'' the founding mints a VEIL TAG (persisted in the daemon doc), derives the creator-veil off the vessel seed, and ''the veil-keyed identity CREATES both WHO-plane sentinels'' — the raw vessel Individual holds no grade anywhere, and the byte-law is witnessed at ceremony grain (''no carried event spells the raw vessel key'', `veil-born-group.test.ts`). The runtime stands ''both identities'' (`operator-daemon-behavior`: the veil boots beside the vessel from the persisted tag) and every vessel-bag→face delegation walks ''ONE ROAD'' (`delegateToFaceViaVeil`: vessel→veil admin edge · veil ingests + adopts · veil seats the bag under the group) — the boot's bag caps, the wiki bindings, the face-join re-grants, and `packPersonaCrossing`'s two-handed seat all ride it. The joinee reads shared content end-to-end (`bind-under-handle` green). ''The JOINEE leg LANDED (same day):'' the joinee derives its veil from the CARRIED group doc id, a veil-keyed card seats and READS (the group's material keys to the seated card's prekeys), the apply persists the doc id AS the veil tag (one boot rule stands either veil), and ''both identities' archives survive restarts'' (`veil-archive.bin` beside the vessel's, witnessed across two live boots). ''Remaining on this road:'' the leaf's summons builder presents the veil card when the leaf wire lands (G5) · the bag-plane creator-cleartext stands as its earlier declared concern · the one-road helper's per-call cost stays unmeasured before G4 multiplies callers. Probes that shaped it: self-eviction REFUSED · any-grade-is-roster · carriage-≠-materialization · the coparent door (upstream pothole). ''Three more doors probed (g1-scope.probe.test.ts):'' READ-GRADE members ride the CGKA too — ANY access is roster membership, no sub-roster grade exists (second confirmation, different angle) · CARRIAGE alone does not materialize a doc — a boot must STAND the veil identity, never merely replay its events (`daemonSeesDoc: false` after a 7-event ingest) · the COPARENT-at-birth door is UNMEASURABLE from JS (the slim binding's Peer marshaling throws an unhandled `__wasm_refgen_toJsPeer` error — an upstream pothole for the donation ledger, beside alpha.8's "Redelagation" spelling) · and ''THE BYTES NAMED THE TRUE SURFACE'' (`host-enumeration-surface.probe.test.ts`): ''the CREATOR's identifier rides every carried event in CLEARTEXT'' — greppable by any host with no keys — while an admitted member's id stayed out of the bystander stream. The byte-level cross-group correlator is the EVENT LOG a carrier holds, not the CGKA roster a member reads; the veil-born design covers it exactly (the veil becomes the creator), which upgrades G1 from privacy-hygiene to byte-measured necessity. The declared red + measured cure ride in `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/veil-on-the-roster.test.ts`.
# ''G2 — the KEL grammar freezes WHOLE. Both gates ANSWERED in prose (2026-09-08, identity-classes):'' the HARDENING RULE stands walked (kapae-reversible provisional authority · veto out-competes causally always · observer-local hardening by silence-across-K-local-epochs · contest-keyed board `{prefix}/{seq}/{eventCid}`, veto-beats-provisional fold) and the GRAMMAR FIT ruled the handle-KEL a SIBLING grammar (own domain, ATTESTATION + terminal BURN kinds, owner-binding at inception — G3 builds it on frozen primitives, no bytes-change). ''THE SETTLEMENT LANDED (same day) — THE GRAMMAR IS FROZEN:'' the provisional marker + the veto kind took the persona-KEL's LAST bytes-change under this alpha (`mintVeto` · `foldPersonaContests` · `headOpKey`'s provisional restraint · the board's contest keying with the veto-beats-provisional fold). All four walked clauses stand witnessed (`provisional-veto.test.ts`): a provisional confers only kapae-reversible authority · a late veto kills a hardened provisional AND its descendants · the contest survives the board un-collapsed · an idle observer's patience is the resting state. Rite green, breath green on the rebuilt binary. From here the KEL changes only by a NEW alpha's word.
# ''G3 — the Face's spine. LIFT 1 LANDED (2026-09-09, `5239399f9`):'' the handle-card's bare-key `nym` retired onto the handle-KEL — `nym` now names the KEL PREFIX (stable across rotate/graft/burn), the card carries its CHAIN signed by the current head, and `verifyHandleCard` gained a TIER axis (Tier-1 self-contained ⊥ Tier-2 owner-head-checked, so a self-contained pass never masquerades as board-checked; rejections chain-invalid·nym-mismatch·burned·owner-head-refused). QR ceiling NAMED (`QR_CARRIAGE_MAX_EVENTS=2`, past it paste/file). On-disk: `HandleBookSnapshot` v2 — a pre-KEL bare-key snapshot DROPS on load (versioned reset, re-TOFU from announces — never the silent catch→new wipe); the lossy old→new reconstruction stands as a declared skip (a bare key is not a chain). ''REMAINING: LIFT 2 (the antigen ban-`nym` + its 64-hex gates → the persona-KEL pin-move, a separate plane) UNTOUCHED by design.'' ✓ ''Joint RESOLVED (owner-model ruling, 2026-09-09):'' the personal face is PERSONA-ANCHORED, not self-owned. The contact-read found ONE owner model, not two — `mintHandleInception` is provably sugar over `mintHandleInceptionSet([owner],1,…)`, so 1-of-1 and k-of-n share one structure. The whole joint was one argument `mintPersonaGlamour` passed: the handle key owning ITSELF (foreclosing recovery — a self-owned member resolves to no persona head). Enacted: `mintPersonaGlamour`/`publishPersonaGlamour` now take `ownerPersonaKelPrefix` and seat the OWNING persona-KEL prefix as the sole owner member; a lost presentation key recovers THROUGH the persona (the owner authorizes a rotation). Red-first (`persona-glamour-anchored.test.ts` 2/2), green across mesh/node/browser. The deliberately-standalone sovereign-handle class stays a NAMED, un-foreclosed door (operator's "pono" left it open, unbuilt). ✓ ''THE GLAMOUR SINK LANDED (2026-09-09): `lares handle publish`'' — the FIRST production caller of `publishPersonaGlamour`, the publicly published "here I am" note (a Handle, operator's pet-name). The scout had found source ✓ (personaKelPrefix persisted + boot-loaded) + seam ✓ (`whoFaceCap.announce`) + sink ✗ (no caller); this closes the sink on the node surface. `runHandlePublish` (node adapter) opens the store, loads the persona seed + prefix, resolves the deterministic WHO board (nexusPubkey = vessel key), and mints+announces; the testable core `publishHandleFromDaemonDoc` reads the prefix and ''FAILS CLOSED when it is absent'' — a face with no persona to own it never self-owns (`handle-publish.test.ts` 2/2, CLI dispatch smoke-checked on the built bin). ''REMAINING sinks:'' the browser publish surface + the phone/QR summons presenting the veil card (G5). ✓ ''ISOMORPHIC MOVE + VERB FAMILY (2026-09-09):'' the publish orchestration (`publishHandleFromDaemonDoc`) moved from the node command INTO `@lararium/mesh` (`handle-publish.ts`), so a phone-only holder (three phones + a friend's Nexus) runs the same act — the node adapter keeps only the disk shores. And the `lares handle` noun now scaffolds its whole family: `publish` LIVE · `rotate` · `graft` · `burn` · `attest` as honest stubs (recognized, print their shape + the mesh mint that stands + the canon pointer, exit 3). The four deep ahu (esp. TRUE k-of-n graft governance, `handle-kel.test.ts:400`) stay DECLARED — loop back to wire each vessel-side orchestration. ✓ ''FORK 1 RESOLVED — the leased-projection core (2026-09-09, after a cross-domain research pass):'' the record-vs-board question ruled toward the BOARD. `handle-orchestration.ts` (mesh, isomorphic) — `resolveOwnHandleChain` reads the authoritative chain off the WHO board (the record stays a thin index; a chain a record OWNED would read as a compiled who-is-X-of-one the registry filter refuses), `extendOwnHandle` LEASE-CHECKS before minting (compare-and-swap: git force-with-lease · KERI accept-on-quorum · SWIM higher-incarnation), so a stale view never forks the name; a partition fork stays caught sovereign at read (HandleBook + equivocation gossip). Red-first (`handle-orchestration.test.ts` 2/2, the lease refuses a moved head with a matching-lease control). This is the reusable pattern the three remaining verbs (rotate/graft/burn/attest orchestration) now mirror — each supplies only its mint + card-build; lease+resolve+announce stay shared. ✓ ''FIRST VERB WIRED — `burnOwnHandle` (2026-09-09):'' the template proven with the simplest verb — an owner-burn (Option C path two: the owning persona buries the face from above) specialized over `extendOwnHandle`, so the burn mints over the board's CURRENT chain and a stale lease refuses it (no name burns from a head the board moved past). Isomorphic mesh core, red-first (`handle-orchestration.test.ts` 4/4: the burned chain verifies terminal · a stale lease refuses). Rotate/graft/attest mirror this shape; the node/CLI adapter (owner-op-key derivation + card re-sign from the persona seed) is the next increment. ''Owed (record-only):'' the CHANGELOG burn bullet waits on the operator's in-flight `place-meme`/`MemeSink` CHANGELOG entry committing first (not folded into the burn commit, to keep isolation).

✓ ''AHI KĀ PROBE LANDED (2026-09-09, `a2ae8f364`):'' `ahi-ka.ts` (isomorphic, observer-local) reads ahi-ka | ahi-tere | ahi-mātaotao | abstain; the discrimination probe (`ahi-ka.test.ts` 4/4, red-first) proves the naive own-steps yardstick false-colds a partition (the control that lies) while the AMBIENT yardstick abstains; ahi tere shows as a RATIO not a duration. Kept SEPARATE from `realm-standing.ts` (verdict-free — a near-clobber recovered: Write onto that taken filename was caught + reverted, lesson in [[feedback-dist-is-shared-mutable]]). Estimator minimal (ratio + abstain floor); NegBin/conformal deferred; the yardstick is injected.

★ ''COLLISION HANDBACK — the roadmap vs the federated-mesh field (2026-09-09).'' The field VALIDATED the shape hard: KERI (KEL + TOAD accept-on-witness-quorum = our leased-projection CAS) · did:plc (authoritative op-log + thin local index, in production; its only residual centralization is TIMESTAMP/ORDER, not identity) · SSB frozen-identity = the measured grave of no-rotation-indirection · Farcaster global IdRegistry + did:key = the compiled-registry / no-rotation graves we forbid · CONIKS = the read-side fork-catch deployed · Θ-model + time-free query-response FD = clockless liveness on a RATIO, proven. ''Refined-plan delta (ranked):'' ① formalize the ambient as the Θ-ratio + drive standing with HashiCorp Lifeguard's FSM (LHM back-off closes the co-driven objection · log-suspicion-decay-by-corroboration = quantified hysteresis+watcher · buddy-first refutation) · ② adopt KERI pre-rotation + TOAD into the verb family (pre-commit next-key digest; CAS = accept-on-quorum) · ③ RESHAPE ④ as a corollary of ①+③ — a Nexus IS a KERI group AID, a joinee learns its key by verifying the group KEL to witness-quorum (no roster), the Nexus key a GROUP key (FROST/KERI multisig) NEVER a shared secret (the SSB fusion grave) · ④ steal Willow range-reconciliation for KEL-fork catching + make "correct even if all timestamps were zero" canon · ⑤ danger-model CO-STIMULATION: never sever a realm/human on a single suspicion (K independent corroborations + a damage signal — the immune answer to the Mastodon-blocklist autoimmune cascade, itself the empirical proof of the registry filter). ''Sharpest insight:'' the last thing the whole field decentralizes is ORDER/TIME — our carriage-liveness ambient is the mesh's replacement for the one primitive everyone else still cheats on (the keystone under the keystone). ''⚠ BIGGEST EXPOSURE (verdict):'' detection (③) cannot PREVENT a LIVE-key equivocator, and KERI has no admin recovery for a live current+next capture — that case falls only to recovery-quorum (⑤), which the roadmap builds LAST; worse, a live equivocator controlling enough carriage triggers the diffusion-sensing/Sybil fool exactly when the attack is live. ''PULL recovery-quorum FORWARD to sit beside ③'' — detection and recovery are each other's blind spot. ''⚠ CANON FORK for the operator (lamplighters):'' `:198` already grounds the fourth option (accrual rides a quantity driven by OTHERS = the ambient) ✓, but `:206` holds that turning a count into a verdict smuggles a RATE (behind = rate = duration) needing a real-time bound R; the collision's Θ-model / time-free-FD literature DISPUTES this (a suspicion verdict from a purely LOGICAL constraint, no real-time R). ''RULED (operator, 2026-09-11): READ FREE, ACT BY CONTRACT.'' The `:206` objection binds only where a CONSEQUENCE hurts a party (dispossession · name-release · eviction · resource-reclaim), and the bound R for such an act lives in the sharing parties' own bilateral contract, ''never a mesh-wide law'' — exactly where `:206` already said the threshold lands. So the reading stays a log-fact plus attenuation ALWAYS: clockless, accusing nobody. `readAhiKa` needed no change; the ruling legalizes the reading it already performed (`api/pono/field-collision#/standing-tensions` · `lararium/mesh/lamplighters`). ''The research's sharpest rhyme, kept:'' Fork 1 (fork a KEL head) and Fork 2 (whitewash a realm) read as ONE attack at two scales — minting a second present that disowns its past — and our equivocation gossip + φ-accrual are one instrument reading it. ''FORK 2 (the realm idle clock / ahi kā erosion) — ENACTED (2026-09-12), and the numbers RATIFIED (2026-09-13).'' The shape holds (three states ahi kā/ahi tere/ahi mātaotao read as a RATIO over causal arrivals, welded to the KEL against whitewash) and it RUNS: `BagStowage` cools by the realm's OWN ROLLS (`DEFAULT_IDLE_ROLLS = 8`, matching ahi kā's `ambientFloor`) and names its `clockKind` — `"realm"` when a realm clock rides in, `"wall-floor"` when